# ©AngelaMos | 2026
# .gitignore.example
#
# Annotated .gitignore template for Cybersecurity-Projects.
# Copy into your project root, rename to `.gitignore`, and delete the
# language sections your stack does not use.
#
# Pattern syntax:
#   file.txt      that name, at any depth
#   *.log         glob
#   /build        anchored: only at the directory holding this .gitignore
#   build/        directories only
#   !keep.txt     re-include something an earlier line excluded
#   **/cache      any depth
#
# A pattern cannot re-include a file whose PARENT directory is excluded:
# `logs/` then `!logs/keep` does not work, `logs/*` then `!logs/keep` does.
#
# Check why a path is ignored:  git check-ignore -v <path>
# Untrack a file you just ignored (keeps it on disk): git rm --cached <path>
#
# Docs: https://git-scm.com/docs/gitignore
# Upstream templates: https://github.com/github/gitignore


# ── Secrets & Environment ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The section that matters most. If a secret is ever committed, ROTATE it.
# Rewriting history does not help: forks, clones and caches already have it.
#
# Public certificates (*.crt, cert.pem, ca.pem) are NOT ignored, because
# test fixtures and CA bundles are legitimately committed. Private keys are,
# including the PEM spellings (key.pem, privkey.pem, mkcert's *-key.pem).

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
key.pem
*-key.pem
*_key.pem
privkey*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
.netrc
.npmrc.local
secrets/*
!secrets/.gitkeep


# ── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

.venv/
venv/

build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
*.egg
wheels/

.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ty_cache/
.pytype/
.pyre/
.hypothesis/

.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
*.prof


# ── Node / TypeScript ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
.pnpm-debug.log*
*.tsbuildinfo
.vite/
.eslintcache
.stylelintcache
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/


# ── Go ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Go emits one binary named after the module or -o flag. Ignore it by name
# (anchored, so a `cmd/<name>/` source directory is not swallowed), and
# uncomment /bin/ only if bin/ holds build output rather than scripts:
# /<binary-name>
# /bin/

__debug_bin*
*.test
*.out
go.work.sum


# ── Rust ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Commit Cargo.lock for binaries AND libraries (Cargo's guidance since 2023).

target/
**/*.rs.bk


# ── Zig ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .zig-cache/ since Zig 0.13; zig-cache/ for older toolchains.

.zig-cache/
zig-cache/
zig-out/


# ── C / C++ ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# compile_commands.json is generated per machine (absolute paths). Symlink it
# from build/ for clangd instead of committing it.

cmake-build-*/
CMakeUserPresets.json
compile_commands.json
.cache/clangd/
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.lib


# ── Nim / Haskell ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

nimcache/
nimblecache/
.stack-work/
dist-newstyle/
.ghc.environment.*


# ── Crystal (uncomment in Crystal projects only) ──────────────────────────────
# shards installs dependencies into lib/. Commented by default: in every
# other language /lib/ is usually real source.
#
# /lib/
# /.shards/


# ── Docker ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Override files are per-machine. Shared config belongs in compose.yml or
# dev.compose.yml.

compose.override.yml
compose.override.yaml
docker-compose.override.yml
docker-compose.override.yaml


# ── Local Databases ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
dump.rdb


# ── Captures & Archives (opt-in) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Security projects deliberately commit pcaps, archives and samples as test
# fixtures, so these stay commented. Uncomment when they are only ever
# runtime output.
#
# *.pcap
# *.pcapng
# *.zip
# *.tar.gz


# ── Editors & AI Tooling ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shared editor settings are a team decision. `.vscode/*` (not `.vscode/`)
# so a single file can still be re-included below.

.vscode/*
# !.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
.zed/
.fleet/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.direnv/
.claude/
CLAUDE.local.md


# ── OS Junk ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.Trash-*
.directory


# ── Logs & Release Artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

*.log
logs/
*.exe
*.dll
*.dylib
